// The curated catalog of known trophies.
//
// Source: BBL's own authoritative trophy legend pages, `default.asp?p=tt`
// (team trophies) and `default.asp?p=ppr` (player trophies) -- confirmed
// exhaustive at 16 + 12 = 28 entries, matching every distinct `gfx/prizeN.gif`
// icon found anywhere in the mirrored BBL dataset. Descriptions are
// translated from the original Swedish. Four further trophies (Ogretoberfest
// and the three Dungeon Bowl placements) are TP-only and have no BBL
// equivalent.
//
// Trophies deliberately carry NO shared "Name" external id, the same precedent
// competitions set: superficially identical labels (e.g. "1st") can be
// genuinely different trophies depending on the competition tier, so identity
// is a curation decision, never inferred from
// label text. BBL's *team* trophy labels ARE self-disambiguating (`Major 1st`
// vs. `Minor 1st`), so each of those is keyed by the exact BBL label text
// itself (matching the raw source id/label convention every other
// curated-data file and every real BBL importer use -- no prefix).
//
// Some of BBL's *player* trophy labels are NOT self-disambiguating: BBL
// hands the same "Deadliest Player" label out in several competition groups,
// so the label alone identifies no single trophy. Every curated row for one
// of these labels -- including its original Major Season row -- is keyed by
// the composite `${label}-${groupName}` BBL external id instead of the bare
// label, the same hyphen-joined composite the tourplay.net ids below use, so
// BblTrophyAwardsImportService's composite-key attempt always resolves them
// regardless of group: there is no Major-Season-specific bare-label
// exception left to be inconsistent about. A handful of other player
// trophies (Bierhallenführer, Gudarnas Förkämpe) are already
// self-disambiguating on their own and keep a bare-label id like team
// trophies do; the importer's composite attempt is expected to miss for
// these, and its bare-label fallback is what actually resolves them. 7
// group-scoped rows carry the Minor Season variants of the "during the
// season" player trophies, which are genuinely per-group recurring awards.
// Legendary Player and Trogen Tjänst are not: they are lifetime
// achievements awarded whenever a player crosses a threshold, in whatever
// competition happens to be running, so each is a single row scoped to the
// league rather than to any group, and each keeps a bare-label BBL external
// id like the self-disambiguating trophies do -- the importer's composite
// attempt misses and its bare-label fallback resolves them. "Season MVP" has
// no group-scoped sibling of its own -- no cross-group award of it is
// confirmed in the cached data, and the server-side group-match check would
// surface one loudly if it ever appeared.
//
// TP external ids are seeded for the 10 trophies TP actually awards, keyed as
// `${disambiguator}-${groupName}` -- the same hyphen-joined composite BBL
// positions use (`${typId}-${race.bblId}`). TP's raw
// `awardType` codes (1/2/3, 100/200) are NOT globally unique per trophy: the
// same code means a different trophy depending on which competition tier it
// appears in, so the competition group's name is what scopes it.
// The disambiguator is the raw award's `name` field when present ("Best
// Stunty", "Wooden Spoon" -- which share one numeric awardType within a file,
// so the name is the only thing that separates them) and the numeric
// `awardType` otherwise (1/2/3).
//
// 10 entries are seeded, confirmed by reading all 13 local TP award files: TP
// has so far only tracked 4 competition groups (Major Season, Chaos Cup,
// Dungeon Bowl, Ogretoberfest). Dungeon Bowl has three catalog trophies of
// its own; BBL never awarded one, so none of these three carry a
// `tloeg.bbleague.se` id. Award files contain placement entries only
// (awardType 1/2/3) with no Best Stunty or Wooden Spoon, so no stunty/spoon
// entries are seeded for Dungeon Bowl. TP's award files have so far only
// contained team-level entries, so none of the 24 player trophies and none of
// the BBL-only cups have any TP source data to ground an id on. Those stay
// unseeded rather than carrying a guessed code -- a new TP competition
// tracking a different group, or a new award kind, would widen this set.
//
// Every competition-scoped trophy also records the competition group it is
// applicable for, so the TP awards importer (tools/import-tp/src/trophy-awards/)
// can consider only applicable trophies when awarding for a competition --
// Legendary Player and Trogen Tjänst are league-scoped instead and carry no
// competition group, as explained below. The eight unqualified "during the
// season" player trophies (Season MVP through
// Most SPP) are curated under Major Season: Major is BBL's flagship season
// and the legend defines no Minor-season equivalent. Their group-scoped
// siblings (see the composite-id note above) carry the other groups BBL
// actually awarded them in. Legendary Player and Trogen Tjänst are
// league-scoped instead, since they are awarded across every group rather
// than tied to one. Bierhallenführer and Gudarnas Förkämpe follow their own
// description text, which is already explicit about the event they are
// awarded at.
//
// Every entry also curates an award rule, classifying how its winner is
// actually determined so missing awards can be computed from imported match
// events rather than left to a human to fill in by hand. Team placement
// trophies and the two trophies no statistic can determine (Season MVP,
// Gudarnas Förkämpe) carry `direct_source`/`manual` plus a prose
// `awardProcedure`. The remaining player trophies are computed: `max_count`
// counts matching match events and takes the acting player with the most;
// `max_spp_sum` sums `match_events.spp_value` instead; `career_threshold`
// awards every player who crosses a lifetime figure. Every `max_count`/
// `max_spp_sum` trophy uses a tie cutoff of 4 -- real BBL data has ties of up
// to four players for these awards, so four is the cutoff across the board,
// not tuned per trophy. Top Fouler/Minor Top Fouler counts foul actions
// outright, regardless of what the foul did: every `foul` match event counts,
// whether or not it caused a casualty. Most SPP/Minor Most SPP
// deliberately curate no included match-event types at all: every
// SPP-bearing event counts toward the sum, including ones outside the
// standardised award table that TP separately reports figures for.
// Bierhallenführer's "the Ogre who..." restriction is modelled as
// `awardRuleEligiblePositions`, alongside its MVP exclusion: without it the
// rule would hand an Ogre-only trophy to whichever non-Ogre happened to top
// the competition's SPP table.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],
  trophies: [
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // Team trophies
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    {
      name: 'Major Gold',
      recipientKind: 'team',
      competitionGroup: { system: 'Name', id: 'Major Season' },
      description: 'Major season winner.',
      awardRuleKind: 'direct_source',
      awardProcedure:
        "Taken from the season's own final standings, as recorded by the source.",
      externalIds: [
        { system: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', id: 'Major 1st' },
        { system: 'tourplay.net', id: '1-Major Season' },
